WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.457 --> 00:00:02.040
SPEAKER 1: What
Joseph will eventually

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:05.970
come to be known for isn't a
dreamer but a reader of dreams.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.442
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.560
"And Jacob dwelled in the land
of his father's sojournings,

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.060
in the land of Canaan.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.160
This is the lineage of Jacob.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.070
Joseph, 17 years old,
was tending the flock

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.130
with his brothers,
assisting the son of Bilhah

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:32.310
and the sons of Zilpah,
the wives of his father.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.340
And Joseph brought ill report
of them to their father.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.980
And Israel loved Joseph
more than all his sons

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.930
for he was a child
of his old age,

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.390
and he made him an
ornamented tunic.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:45.960
And his brother saw it was their
father who loved Joseph more

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.140
than all his brothers and
they hated him and could not

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:52.320
speak a kind word to him."

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.840
My students are
often taken aback

00:00:54.840 --> 00:01:00.200
because Joseph brought ill
report of them to their father.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:03.320
Students often wonder, is
this just the youngest brother

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.660
being a snitch?

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:08.210
Hold on to that because I
think the text later will

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:11.240
start to answer our question.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.550
Oftentimes, we think
that the brothers simply

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:16.250
despise Joseph because
of his ornamented tunic.

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:20.000
But the text sets it up that
the ornamented tunic is actually

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.110
a representation of
his favorite status.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:27.050
"And Joseph dreamed a dream
and told it to his brothers

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:29.240
and they hated him all the more.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.970
And he said to them,
'Listen, pray to this dream

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:32.630
that I dreamed.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:35.300
And look, we were binding
sheaves in the field, and look,

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.060
my sheaf arose and actually
stood up, and look,

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.570
your sheaves drew round
and bowed to my sheaf.'

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:45.320
And his brother said to him,
'Do you mean to reign over us?

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:47.420
Do you mean to rule us?'

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:50.330
And they hated him all
the more for his dreams

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:51.840
and for his words."

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.260
There are a few interesting
things going on here.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.080
What Joseph will eventually
come to be known for

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.960
isn't a dreamer but
a reader of dreams.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:02.840
Here, we begin in
the narrative, we

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:06.740
see Joseph himself
is the dreamer.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.120
"And he dreamed
yet another dream

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.500
and recounted it
to his brothers.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.625
And said, 'Look, I dreamed
a dream again, and look,

00:02:11.625 --> 00:02:14.840
the sun and the moon and the 11
stars were bowing down to me.'

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.180
And he recounted it to his
father and to his brothers.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:18.850
And his father
rebuked him and said,

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.600
'What is this dream
that you have dreamed?

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:23.420
Shall we really come, I and
your mother and your brothers,

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.120
to bow down before
you to the ground?'

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.040
And his brothers
were jealous of him,

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.620
while his father kept
the thing in mind."

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:35.060
And again, we do not get his
understanding of this dream.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:39.650
It's just these enigmatic
dreams at this point.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:42.140
"And his brothers went to
graze their father's flock

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:42.950
at Shechem.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:45.560
And Israel said to
Joseph, 'You know,

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.540
your brothers are
pastoring at Shechem.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.640
Come let me send you to them.'

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:52.820
And he said to him, 'Here I am.'

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:56.060
And he said, 'Go pray to see
how your brothers fare and how

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.540
the flocks fare and
bring me back word.'"

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.420
Ah, now we get to
see perhaps that

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:05.180
which preceded
there in Chapter 37

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:09.290
that Joseph isn't bringing ill
report just in and of himself.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:12.650
It's his father who's
asking him to go and look

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:16.190
after his brothers to see
how the flock is faring.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:20.300
And, of course, he goes and
he looks for his brothers.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.510
"And they saw him from
afar before he drew near,

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.290
and they plotted against
him to put him to death.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:30.650
And they said to each other,
'Here comes that dream master.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:34.230
And so now, let us kill him and
fling him into one of the pits.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.770
And we can say a vicious
beast has devoured him,

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.020
and we shall see what
comes of his dreams.'"

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:40.940
I find this moment fascinating.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:43.730
One, notice, they're
all speaking together.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:45.080
Each said to each other.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.930
It's as if they're speaking
in a unified manner.

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:49.940
And I find this
fascinating because what

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:52.880
you saw in the dream were
all of the sheaves on one

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:56.420
side and Joseph there
against all the others.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:58.670
And this is going to play
out in the narrative for us.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:03.920
All the brothers united
against one brother

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:09.440
who is, in fact, the
beloved of his father.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:12.110
"And Reuben heard and came
to his rescue and said,

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.060
'We must not take his life.'

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.700
And Reuben said to
them, 'Shed no blood.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:19.459
Fling him into this pit in the
wilderness and do not raise

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:22.880
a hand against him,' so that
Reuben might rescue him from

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:25.430
their hands to bring
him back to his father."

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:26.850
We have to stop here.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:29.090
I think this is a
really important detail

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:30.080
in the narrative.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.930
First off, you have to realize
Reuben is the eldest son.

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:36.082
Whatever favoritism is
being heaped upon Joseph,

00:04:36.082 --> 00:04:37.790
this really is something
that ought to be

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:40.070
going to Reuben as first born.

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:44.570
And so now, think about what
happens if Reuben's plan comes

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:45.470
to fruition.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:46.460
What happens?

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:47.600
Just think about it.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.090
All the brothers over
here versus Joseph

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:51.840
the one over here.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.720
And then they fling
him into the pit,

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:57.350
and then Reuben rescues him and
brings him back to his father

00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:00.650
so that Reuben can stand there
in solidarity with Joseph,

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:03.560
his father's beloved
son, and perhaps

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:06.890
get some of Joseph's favoritism,
some of the light that shines

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:09.890
on Joseph to shine a little bit
on Reuben who, of course, has

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.320
fallen out of his
father's good graces.

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:14.565
"And it happened when
Joseph came to his brothers

00:05:14.565 --> 00:05:16.940
that they stripped him of his
tunic, the ornamented tunic

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:17.810
that he had on him.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.685
And they took him and
flung him into the pit,

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:20.850
and the pit was empty.

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:21.933
There was no water in it.

00:05:21.933 --> 00:05:24.350
And they sat down to eat bread,
and they raised their eyes

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:26.660
and saw and, look, a
caravan of Ishmaelites

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:29.720
was coming bearing gum and
balm and ladanum on their way

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.100
down to Egypt.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.170
And Judah said to
his brothers, 'What

00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:36.560
gain is there if we kill our
brother and cover up his blood?

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.350
Come, let us sell him to the
Ishmaelites and our hand will

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:43.460
not be against him for he is
our brother, our own flesh.'"

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:45.230
And it's important
to take note here

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:47.990
that it is, in fact,
Judah is the one who

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:50.990
wants to find some
sort of material gain

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:53.600
in selling Joseph into slavery.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:55.070
Just take note of
that because this

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:59.240
is going to become important
at the end of the story.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:02.240
"And his brothers agreed, and
they sold Joseph into Egypt.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:04.340
And then Reuben came
back to the pit and look,

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.863
Joseph was not in the pit,
and he rent his garments,

00:06:06.863 --> 00:06:08.780
and he came back to his
brothers, and he said,

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:11.540
'The boy is gone, and
I, where can I turn?'

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:15.170
And they took Joseph's
tunic and slaughtered a kid

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:17.360
and dipped the tunic
in blood, and they

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:20.420
sent the ornamented tunic and
had brought it to their father,

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:22.790
saying, 'This is a
beautiful moment.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:25.820
Recognize, pray, is it
your son's tunic or not?'

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:29.132
And he recognized it, and he
said, 'It is my son's tunic.'"

00:06:29.132 --> 00:06:30.590
Just think about
this for a moment.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:33.350
They're showing this
kind of condensed symbol

00:06:33.350 --> 00:06:35.900
of their father's favoritism.

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:39.660
And he can see it
standing of Joseph

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:42.980
who's gone but also
that condensed symbol

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:47.395
of their brother's hatred for
him of his favored status.

00:06:47.395 --> 00:06:49.780
"And Jacob rent his clothes
and put on sackcloth

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:53.200
round his waist and mourn
for his son many days.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.110
And all his sons and all his
daughters rose to console him,

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:57.790
and he refused to be
consoled and said,

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:02.650
'Rather, I will go down to my
son in Sheol mourning,' and he

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:05.110
keened for him."

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.560
SPEAKER 2: Thank
you for watching.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:08.530
We hope you're enjoying
our Highlight Series

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:11.410
and invite you to explore
all of Hillsdale College's

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:12.610
online courses.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:16.770
They are free and for
everyone who loves to learn.

